# Generated output — written by a tool, so Prettier must not own its formatting.
# Otherwise `npm run format` and the generator rewrite the file against each
# other and CI's `git diff --exit-code` fails every run.
#
# They reach conformance by three different routes, which is why all three are
# listed rather than trusting the two that pass today:
#   schema.json      `sanity schema extract` writes it space-indented while
#                    .prettierrc sets useTabs. This is the one that already bites.
#   sanity.types.ts  formatted by @sanity/codegen's own bundled Prettier — a
#                    version alignment that a codegen bump can break.
#   groq-constants   emitted by scripts/generate-groq-constants.mjs as a plain
#     .generated.ts  template literal, never touched by Prettier. It conforms
#                    only because the template was hand-written that way, so
#                    editing that template is what would drift it.
# Keep in step with the generated set in .github/workflows/checks.yml.
schema.json
sanity.types.ts
src/sanity/lib/groq-constants.generated.ts
# drizzle-kit writes its migration snapshots space-indented, like schema.json.
drizzle/meta/

# Each worktree is a second full checkout with its OWN .prettierrc, so without
# this `prettier .` descends into them: +1.8s, thousands of "[warn] Ignored
# unknown option" lines, and `npm run format` rewriting another branch's working
# tree under that branch's config. Scoped to worktrees/ deliberately — `.claude/`
# would also exempt the tracked .claude/launch.json and .claude/rules/*.md, which
# should stay formatted. Prettier needs its own entry because it reads
# .gitignore, and .claude/worktrees/ is excluded via .git/info/exclude.
.claude/worktrees/
